| Bug | Root cause | Fix |
|-----|-----------|-----|
| Heading ignored later parent changes | `connectedCallback` overwrote the `@api` property with the upper-cased value | Removed the mutation; introduced a `displayHeading` getter that upper-cases on the fly |
| Component mutated the parent's array / task objects | `this.items = this.tasks` was a shallow reference; toggle pushed/mutated in-place | `@api` **setter** deep-copies (`map(t => ({...t})); all mutations produce a new array via spread / `map` |
| New tasks didn't appear / counter didn't update (and console error) | Mutating a property on an object inside an array does not trigger LWC re-render; `event.target.dataset.id` could also mismatch on numeric IDs | Reassign `this._tasks` to a **new array** in both `handleAdd` and `handleToggle`; use `event.currentTarget.dataset.id` with a `String()` comparison |
| Parent never hears about new tasks | Event name was `'taskAdded'` (camelCase); `detail.label` was read *after* `this.newLabel` was reset to `''` | Dispatch `'taskadded'` (lowercase) with the label captured *before* clearing |
